From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Odin 3: offer every refresh rate from 30 to 120Hz

The odin3 kernel adds an ICNA3520 mode for each integer rate from 30 to
120Hz (patch 0138), so the panel can run at any of them natively. The quirk
pinned the Odin 3 to 60 and 120, which left those modes unused.

This is what ran on the device from 2026-08-12 as a user environment.d
override; it moves into the session so the image carries it.
---
--- a/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/device-quirks
+++ b/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/device-quirks
@@ -307,11 +307,13 @@
 
 if [[ ":AYN Odin 3:" =~ ":$SYS_ID:" ]]; then
   ORIENTATION=right
-  CUSTOM_REFRESH_RATES=60,120
+  # The odin3 kernel carries a 30..120Hz mode for every integer rate (patch
+  # 0138), so the whole range is real panel modes rather than generated ones.
+  CUSTOM_REFRESH_RATES=30-120
   OUTPUT_CONNECTOR='*,DSI-1'
   FAKE_OUTPUT_MM=177x100
 
-  export STEAM_DISPLAY_REFRESH_LIMITS=60,120
+  export STEAM_DISPLAY_REFRESH_LIMITS=30,120
 fi
 
 if [[ ":AYN Thor:" =~ ":$SYS_ID:" ]]; then
